            "english_quote": "to which the soul, as I said, succumbs and, both sharing the suffering body’s pain and keeping its own understanding occupied, is subjected.",
            "issue": "The Greek makes ἀσχολεῖ the finite predicate: the soul, falling under these passions and sharing the suffering body's pain, also occupies its own understanding. The draft instead makes this central assertion subordinate through “keeping” and ends by repeating the subjection already represented by “succumbs.” Although the constituent meanings are present, their relationship and the sentence's culminating assertion are obscured. This is a translation problem, not evidence of source corruption.",
